<plan steps="Client|Cache|Queue"/>A request starts at the <node id="client" label="Client" kind="actor"/>client, then the <node id="api" label="API" near="client" fill="lilac"/>API checks the <node id="redis" label="Redis" kind="db" near="api" fill="Blush"/><edge from="api" to="redis"/>cache. Writes go through the <node id="jobs" label="Jobs" kind="queue" near="api" dir="below" fill="plaid"/>jobs queue. <compare title="Redis vs Memcached" options="Redis|Memcached" criteria="Latency|Persistence"/>Two options. <cell option="Redis" criterion="Persistence" mark="yes"/><cell row="Latency" col="Memcached" text="sub-ms"/><cell criterion="Redis" option="Latency" mark="no"/>Only Redis persists. <code path="internal/user/service.go" lines="42-52"/>In the code, line 43 <annotate line="43" code="s.cache.Get("/>asks Redis first, and line 44 <annotate line="44" mark="circle"/>returns. <annotate line="0"/>Never mind. <recap bullets="Reads try Redis first|A miss reads Postgres and writes back|TTLs bound staleness"/>To recap.
- The client->CDN hop is **cached** at the *edge*.
## Then API→Redis→Postgres, see _service.go_.
